# Paths that produce collateral merge damage when parallel agents touch them.
#
# Read this before dispatching concurrent work-issue agents. Two pending issues
# whose predicted scopes both intersect a line here are serialized, not
# parallelized. See ~/.claude/skills/work-issue/SKILL.md, "Pre-flight checks".
#
# The cost of getting this wrong is not a merge conflict -- a conflict is loud
# and cheap. It is a plausible-looking resolution that silently breaks an
# invariant nobody re-checks, in a file whose whole job is to be the invariant.

# The closed step vocabulary, and the Python<->C# contract built on it.
# A test asserts the parser implements exactly this file, so a merge that keeps
# "both sides" of a concurrent edit produces a catalogue that still parses,
# still passes locally, and no longer describes what the C# runner binds.
# MARVEL-139 and MARVEL-141 both land here.
py_src/specs/steps.catalogue.json

# Generated ledgers, written only by the validation runner, never by hand.
# Two spec-authoring agents regenerate these from different partial worlds and
# each one's output looks authoritative. Run one spec author at a time.
py_src/specs/trusted.json
py_src/specs/quarantine.json

# One function, several open issues about different ends of the same ordering
# problem: targets are chosen before payment exists. MARVEL-133 and MARVEL-140
# both land here and will disagree about what the fix is.
py_src/game/effect/effect_checker.py
py_src/game/effect/effect_target_cost.py

# Generated card data. Regenerating it moves counts that prose all over the repo
# restates, so an agent that refreshes it invalidates the measurements another
# agent is mid-way through correcting. MARVEL-142 and MARVEL-144 are exactly
# this pair.
datasets/cards/**
datasets/marvelsdb/**

# Carries its own checksum, verified by Json.LoadInternal. Any edit has to
# regenerate it, and two independent regenerations do not merge.
py_src/data/cards.json

# Coverage prose and the tool that produces the numbers it quotes. Anything
# refreshing counts touches both, and so does anything changing what is counted.
py_src/tools/spec/coverage.py
py_src/tools/coverage/reach.py
docs/spec-campaign.md
